//Mentor posts for accelerated turns
var mentorposts = [

"Turn 0",

// Turn 1
"\
Hi all; welcome to the Mentor vs Midshipmen game! In this area you will find messages from your mentor, so be sure to check here for tips and advice. And if you have any questions, just post them here to the Public Board and I'll do my best to answer them!\
<br/>\
<br/>You can go ahead and play your first 5 turns now. Then, once everyone has joined the game will combine everyone's orders and we'll run turns daily after that.\
<br/>\
<br/>Anyways, where to start? On this first turn, the most important things to do are as follows:\
<br/>- At your starbase, build a Large Deep Space Freighter (LDSF) with Transwarp engines.\
<br/>- Load your Medium Deep Space Freighter (MDSF) with 140 colonists, 60 supplies, and 120 megacredits.\
<br/>- Send your MDSF to a nearby planet at Warp 9.  It should be able to reach it in one turn.\
<br/>- On your homeworld, build as many factories as you can.  You'll also need to build some mineral mines, probably up to 300 or so.\
<br/>- Consider taxing your colonists a little to make some extra megacredits early. It can come in handy.\
<br/>\
<br/>Make sure you always hit End Turn when you're finished issuing orders; And this turn, it will take us immediately to turn 2!\
<br/>\
<br/>For a detailed guide to the first turn, check this out if you have time:\
<br/><a href='http://play.planets.nu/#/howtoplay/g-first-turn' target=_blank>http://play.planets.nu/#/howtoplay/g-first-turn</a>\
<br/>\
<br/>Good luck!\
",

// Turn 2
"\
<br/>Welcome back to Turn 2!\
<br/>\
<br/>Hopefully, most of you built a Large Freighter and flew your Medium to a nearby planet.  If you didn't, do it now; better late than never.\
<br/>\
<br/>During the first few turns, your chief goal is to explore your immediate area.  You're hoping to find a good native world so you can tax them and ship their money home.  A moderate climate (near 50) is good and large populations with advanced government is better, but don't be too picky.  Every good native planet needs a ton of your colonists (to help with tax collection).  The only bad natives are Amorphous, since they don't pay taxes and like to snack on your colonists.\
<br/>\
<br/>Even planets with no natives can be good; you need minerals too, and every planet can be mined and support factories.\
<br/>\
<br/>So, first and foremost, go to your Medium Freighter on the starmap and click to see what its planet is like.  If it's a great one, you'll want to remember to send your Large Freighter here immediately with a ton of colonists; otherwise, you can send that out to explore in a different direction instead.\
<br/>\
<br/>Either way, drop a bunch of colonists and supplies from your Medium and move it along to the next world.  For native worlds, you'll need fewer supply units than for non-native.  Empty worlds can also benefit from an infusion of cash; to beam that down to an unowned planet, you'll need to set the friendly code BDM.\
<br/>\
<br/>Next, go to your Large Freighter.  If the planet you found was a great native world, load it with 100 supplies and the rest colonists and send it there right away.  Otherwise, you'll want to load it with more supplies -- 300 is a good number -- and send it out to explore in the other direction.  Don't forget fuel!\
<br/>\
<br/>You'll want to check on your homeworld too.  On the planet's surface, you may be able to build more factories; at the starbase, you'll probably want to build a second Large Freighter.  (Some people build something else, but a second LDSF is usually a good idea.)  If you're running low on money after you build your ship, you may have to go back down to the planet and tax your colonists, but be careful not to tax them too much.  They get very unhappy when you take all their money, and happy colonists are productive colonists.\
<br/>\
<br/>For a more detailed guide to the second turn, look here:\
<br/><a href='http://play.planets.nu/#/howtoplay/g-second-turn' target=_blank>http://play.planets.nu/#/howtoplay/g-second-turn</a>\
",

// Turn 3
"\
<br/>If things have gone well, you've colonized your first planet.  Go there first; you'll see it's a lot like your homeworld, and things can be done the same way.\
<br/>\
<br/>Some rules of thumb for developing your colonies:\
<br/>- Always build factories first, as many as you can.  The supplies they produce are what you'll use to build mines and defense posts.\
<br/>- Don't tax your colonists unless the planet is too hot or too cold to grow your population, or unless there's an emergency.  It's easier to grow them than to ship them here.\
<br/>- If you have good natives (not Amorphous), always tax them.  You need the money here to build structures (and maybe a starbase) and back home to build more ships.  Remember:  The taxes you can collect are limited by the number of colonists you have.\
<br/>\
<br/>Plus one more:\
<br/>    - Try to always have your ships doing something useful if you can.  When you're moving colonists out, sometimes you can move minerals or cash back home.  In this game, you're going to bring minerals to your homeworld to keep building ships.\
<br/>\
<br/>    Speaking of shipbuilding:  Some players swear by building lots of freighters in the early game, and use Larges to ship out loads of colonists, a thousand or so clans at a time, to a single planet with a near-50 climate.  Then they use that world as a staging area for further expansion, leaving a Medium there to spread the wealth around to the local worlds while the Large Freighter goes back for more.  That often means building one or two Mediums for every Large.\
<br/>\
<br/>    Some of you might do better with a different kind of ship, depending on your race.  There are some general suggestions at this link:\
<br/><a href='http://play.planets.nu/#/howtoplay/g-early-ships' target=_blank>http://play.planets.nu/#/howtoplay/g-early-ships</a>\
",

// Turn 4
"\
Hopefully by now you've found at least one good planet with Natives on it; you need a nearby planet to start earning you some tax money so you can afford to keep building ships.\
<br/>\
<br/>If you found one, it's vital that you rush clans there to help collect taxes; most of the time, a planet can only generate one MC per colonist, no matter how many natives there are.  As soon as you find one, load a Large Freighter up with 1100 clans and 100 supplies and move there as fast as you can.  Then, tax the natives and ship the money home.\
<br/>\
<br/>With your other ships, continue to scout and colonize the nearby planets, heading home for more colonists when needed. We want to start looking for a location for a second starbase. Building a second starbase is very important to allow you to build small useful ships for further scouting, moving around money and minerals, and performing special functions like the Lizard Hiss! mission. Your homeworld will continue to build your big important ships.\
<br/>\
<br/>The best planets for second starbases will have Ghipsoldal natives so you instantly get Tech 10 engines on your new starbase. Humanoids are also excellent since they get you free Tech 10 hulls. Other good options are Amphibian (beams) and Siliconoid (torps).  Do your best to find a Ghip or a Humanoid as soon as you can.\
<br/>\
<br/>At this point you should probably think about building a medium warship to use as a forward scout.  If an unarmed enemy freighter accidentally runs into it, or if it happens on lightly-defended enemy planets, it'll pretty much win by default.  When in doubt, take another look at that guide I linked last turn:\
<br/><a href='http://play.planets.nu/#/howtoplay/g-early-ships' target=_blank>http://play.planets.nu/#/howtoplay/g-early-ships</a>\
",

// Turn 5
"\
<br/>Turn 5: This is the last turn of the accelerated start period. When you click 'End Turn' this time, we'll wait a bit for the other players, perhaps as long as a day or two.  Then we'll see what everyone's positions look like and continue from there.  If you want to play some more Planets while you are waiting, I recommend checking out the Levels tab on your main account page. The single player levels there you can play as fast as you want. And if you have any questions now is a good time to ask, and this is a great place!\
<br/>\
<br/>Logistical planning will now start to become very important. At this stage in the game it is vital to continue to build good useful ships every turn you can. Either build your good cargo cruiser or, if you don't have enough resources, another freighter.  Also, we want to get that second starbase up right away, and that will cost minerals and money as well.\
<br/>\
<br/>To make sure you have enough resources you need to plan at least one turn ahead on your resource moving. So this turn you are building one ship. But next turn what ship will you want to build? Will you have enough resources for it?\
<br/>\
<br/>It's also important that, if you have any planets with native life where you are getting less than the max amount of money, you need to move clans there.\
<br/>\
<br/>Another thing to remember is to build factories and mines as quickly as possible on your planets -- especially mines where there are good resources. This map has quite a lot of minerals (senior officer games have less) so there is a lot to mine.\
<br/>\
<br/>And one last thing:  Keep those ships moving usefully as much as you can.\
"

];


function hullImg(hullId, beams) { return vgap.hullImg(hullId, false, beams); }
function hullLeftImg(hullId, beams) { return vgap.hullImg(hullId, true, beams); }
function raceIcon(raceId) { return "http://play.planets.nu/img/races/" + raceId + ".png"; }
function getSoundPath(filename) { return "http://play.planets.nu/audio/" + filename; }
function galleryImage(imgId) { return "http://gallery.planets.nu/" + imgId; }
function galleryThumb(imgId) { return "http://gallery.planets.nu/thumbs/" + imgId; }
function cutSceneImage(imgId) {
    if (imgId == 0)
        return "http://play.planets.nu/img/ui/logo600.png";
    else if (imgId == 13)
        return "http://play.planets.nu/img/story/brokenplanet.jpg";
    else if (imgId == 14)
        return "http://play.planets.nu/img/story/portals.jpg";
    else if (imgId == 15)
        return "http://play.planets.nu/img/backgrounds/space-dock-opt.jpg";
    else
        return "http://play.planets.nu/img/trainers/" + imgId + ".png";
}

function gsv(val) {
    if (val < 0)
        return "?";
    else
        return val;
}

function clone(obj) {
    if (null == obj || "object" != typeof obj) return obj;
    var copy = obj.constructor();
    for (var attr in obj) {
        if (obj.hasOwnProperty(attr)) copy[attr] = obj[attr];
    }
    return copy;
}

